      "id": "bbc-2026-09-18-thames-water-rescue-deal-should-be-rejected-mps",
      "title": "Thames Water rescue deal should be rejected - MPs",
      "summary": "A report on the future of Thames Water, urging the government to take action, has been published.",
      "body": "A cross-party committee of MPs has urged the government to reject a £10bn takeover proposal from Thames Water's creditors.The UK's biggest water company owes roughly £20bn and has been working with creditors and government officials.A report by the Environment, Food and Rural Affairs (EFRA) Committee has now said the government should consider placing it into special administration, a form of temporary nationalisation.A Thames Water spokesperson said it needed to be \"recapitalised and put on a firm financial footing\".Fears that the firm, which serves 16 million customers, could collapse first emerged three years ago.The committee said a takeover plan by a consortium of more than 100 of its creditors did not have \"the interests of the public, the company or the environment at heart\".The plan was seen as the final realistic option to avoid a special administration regime, after a previous deal with a US private equity giant collapsed.Creditors, who collectively own about £17bn of Thames Water's debt, were previously warned by former environment secretary Emma Reynolds their plan did not go far enough to protect customers or the environment.The new report said Thames Water, alongside other \"poor-performing\" water companies, was in a \"doom loop\" of fines for poor performance leaving it with less money to invest in improvements.",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "business",
      "tags": [],
      "author": null,
      "publishedAt": "2026-09-18T05:16:57.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/branded_news/1200/cpsprodpb/d090/live/59b31070-b2b8-11f1-a430-4d16ee157c41.png",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6qjk9q1wpqeo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss",
