      "id": "bbc-2026-09-18-watch-tiny-organisms-on-show-in-microscopic-video-competitio",
      "title": "Watch: Tiny organisms on show in microscopic video competition",
      "summary": "The winning video features tiny hair-like structures, called cilia, in the airways of a child with a rare genetic disease.",
      "body": "Nikon's annual Small World In Motion competition is open to anyone around the world with an interest in film or time-lapse photography through a microscope.This year's winning video was magnified to 100 times in size, and featured tiny hair-like structures, called cilia, in the airways of a child with a rare genetic disease.It was submitted by Dr Ning Xu, a researcher at Tsinghua University in China, who used a series of complicated light waves to illuminate different parts of the sample in colour.Runners up in the competition included videos of a roundworm encountering a single-celled organism and microscopic jellyfish larvae suspended in droplets of water. Clips of bioluminescent algae and a tiny sea slug were among the highly commended.",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "world",
      "tags": [],
      "author": null,
