      "id": "bbc-2026-09-16-british-american-author-and-critic-bonnie-greer-dies-aged-77",
      "title": "British-American author and critic Bonnie Greer dies aged 77",
      "summary": "Her husband says the playwright and cultural and political commentator died after a brief illness.",
      "body": "Speaking to the Guardian, external in 2016 in the aftermath of the Black Lives Matter movement, Greer said: \"When I wake up in the morning, I'm just myself. It's only when I leave the door that I become a black woman to the world.\"She added: \"I tell black women all the time, 'Don't apologise for yourself and keep your hair nappy. Make sure you are heard'.\"Greer served on the boards of cultural institutions including the British Museum, Royal Opera House and London Film School, and was chancellor of London's Kingston University.Her other published works include a memoir titled A Parallel Life and a biography of US poet and playwright Langston Hughes.Also in 2009, her part-memoir, part-music-history book, Obama Music, was published.Greer was made an OBE in 2010 for services to the arts.In 2022, she was appointed as a fellow of the Royal Society of Literature.Broadcaster and author John Simpson added to the tributes on Wednesday, posting: \"So sad to hear of the death of the writer and critic Bonnie Greer.\"She was a good friend, and gave me strong support at a time I needed it. Fiercely intelligent, but always avoided personal attacks. A huge loss.\"Fellow journalist and broadcaster Sangita Myska, who interviewed Greer several times, recalled her as having been a \"smart, sassy, firebrand who will be missed from our public discourse\".",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "world",
      "tags": [],
      "author": null,
      "publishedAt": "2026-09-16T12:41:03.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/branded_news/1200/cpsprodpb/47d1/live/24e2e0d0-b1ed-11f1-a430-4d16ee157c41.jpg",
