      "body": "Home            News            Sport            Weather            iPlayer            Sounds            Bitesize     CBeebies     CBBC     Food         Home     News     Sport     Business     Technology     Health     Culture     Arts     Travel     Earth     Audio     Video     Live          Use BBC.com or the new BBC App to listen to BBC podcasts, Radio 4 and the World Service outside the UK.Find out how to listen to other BBC stationsEpisode detailsWorld Service,·15 Sep 2026,·26 minsAvailable for over a yearAI is developing rapidly. What should parents and children make of it all? And how can young people navigate school and future careers when AI is becoming increasingly important? We speak to an expert who has written a new book about these issues.\nAlso this week: we find out how one piece of health tech is helping scientists uncover disease-fighting data in menstrual blood. And satellite imaging is used by conservationists in Indonesia to protect the habitat of a rare species of orangutan.\n(Photo: A female school pupil sits at a laptop in a computer lab. She is wearing headphones. Credit: Getty Images)Programme WebsiteMore episodes",
